    "evidence_text": "However, no systematic study has previously tested this hypothesis in whole animals.\n\nAgDscam responds to infection by producing pathogen challenge-specific splice form repertoires.\n\nAlphavirus-derived small RNAs modulate pathogenesis in disease vector mosquitoes.\n\nDecreased survival was observed in mosquitoes in which the accumulation of viRNAs was suppressed.\n\nBeta interferon controls West Nile virus infection and pathogenesis in mice.\n\nHowever, the specific functions of individual IFN subtypes remain uncertain.\n\nDuring the mosquito blood-feeding process, WNV infection was blocked in vivo with mosGCTL-1 antibodies.\n\nHowever, An.\n\ngambiae has been shown to be refractory to DNV dissemination.\n\ngambiae.\n\ngambiae using a two-plasmid helper-transducer system.\n\ngambiae mosquitoes.\n\nWild-type and EGFP-transducing AgDNV virions were highly infectious to An.\n\ngambiae.\n\nWNV sequences in mosquitoes were significantly more genetically diverse than WNV in birds.\n\nEvidence of purifying selection was obtained from both intra- and interhost WNV populations.\n\nWest Nile virus (WNV) is a major cause of mosquito-borne illness in the United States.\n\nHuman disease ranges from mild febrile illness to severe fatal neurologic infection.",
